Stressing that all operations by security forces, including those conducted jointly with foreign security personnel, must be carried out in full compliance with international humanitarian law and international human rights law, and underlining the need for accountability for violations and abuses,
Reaffirming the importance of fair and clear procedures for the imposition, review and removal of sanctions, including effective delisting procedures, and recalling the relevant provisions of resolution 2374 (2017),
