Determining that the situation in Mali continues to constitute a threat to international peace and security,
Acting under Chapter VII of the Charter of the United Nations,
1. Decides to renew until 31 August 2024 the measures imposed by paragraphs 1 to 7 of resolution 2374 (2017), as renewed by resolutions 2423 (2018), 2480 (2019), 2541 (2020), 2590 (2021) and 2649 (2022), and reaffirms that the provisions of paragraphs 8 to 13 of resolution 2374 (2017) shall continue to apply, and decides to conduct a review of the measures by 29 February 2024, taking into account the request of the Transition Government of Mali and progress on the benchmarks set out in resolution 2374 (2017), with a view to considering appropriate adjustments, including, as appropriate, suspension or lifting;
2. Reaffirms that the measures set out in resolution 2374 (2017) continue to apply to individuals and entities designated by the Committee established pursuant to resolution 2374 (2017), and calls upon all Member States to implement those measures fully;
