6. Calls upon the Transition Government of Mali to cooperate fully with the United Nations, including the Panel of Experts, and to ensure the safety and security of United Nations personnel, facilities and assets during the drawdown, withdrawal and liquidation of MINUSMA, including by fully respecting the Status of Forces Agreement, including freedom of movement, until the departure of the final element of MINUSMA;
7. Reaffirms that the measures renewed by this resolution are not intended to have adverse humanitarian consequences for the civilian population of Mali, and recalls the humanitarian exemptions and authorisation procedures set out in resolution 2374 (2017) and subsequent resolutions, and the applicability of resolution 2664 (2022);
8. Urges the Transition Government of Mali to make progress on the implementation of the Agreement, the fight against impunity, the promotion and protection of human rights and compliance with international humanitarian law, the protection of civilians, safe, timely and unhindered humanitarian access, the full, equal and meaningful participation of women, and the return to constitutional order, and affirms its intention to keep the sanctions measures under review, including in light of progress in those areas and cooperation with the Panel of Experts and MINUSMA’s drawdown, withdrawal and liquidation, with a view to adjusting or lifting them in light of progress, and requests the Committee, pursuant to its guidelines, to review the list of designated individuals and entities by 29 February 2024, with a view to delisting those who no longer meet the criteria;
9. Calls upon the Transition Government of Mali to ensure that all military and security operations, including those involving foreign private military and security personnel, are conducted in full compliance with international human rights law and international humanitarian law, and to hold perpetrators of violations and abuses accountable;
10. Encourages continued engagement by the United Nations, the African Union, ECOWAS and other regional and international partners in support of Mali’s peace and stabilization efforts, including the implementation of the Agreement and the transition to constitutional order;
11. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

